FINDINGS:
1. [BLOCKER] src/formatter.rs:416 — `write_keyword_line("catch ")` already consumes the trailing comment on the catch line (src/formatter.rs:757), then `self.write(var)` appends the variable after it, producing `catch // commenterr` — why it matters: a `catch err // note` program is corrupted into unparseable output, breaking idempotence and losslessness — concrete fix: do not route `catch` through `write_keyword_line`; write indent + "catch " + var first, then a single `write_trailing_comment`.
2. [MAJOR] src/formatter.rs:287 — block-open lines (`if … then` at :287, `to`/`while`/`for each`/`object`/`try`/`test`) never call `write_trailing_comment` for their own line, so `if 1 is 1 then // note` is re-attached after the whole statement (`end // note`) — why it matters: trailing comments migrate out of their block/line, a silent lossy move with zero covering tests — concrete fix: emit `write_trailing_comment(open_line)` immediately after each block-open line before `newline()`.
3. [MAJOR] src/lib.rs:202 — the `rb format --check` branch (`formatter::needs_reformat`) is never exercised end-to-end: tests/formatter_test.rs:1080 only calls `run_rb("format", …)` plus the pure `needs_reformat` unit, and `run_rb` cannot express `format --check` — why it matters: a regression in the CLI branch (e.g. reintroducing `trim()`) would keep all 51 tests green — concrete fix: add a test that shells `rb format --check <file>` and asserts exit 1/0 on the trailing-whitespace/newline cases from REPORT.md.
4. [MAJOR] tests/formatter_test.rs:118 — `strip_spans` strips spans by naive `find("Span { ")` / `find(" }")` on the `Debug` string, so any program containing that text (e.g. `say "Span { foo }"`) corrupts the comparison — why it matters: `same_program`, the core losslessness oracle, can false-pass or false-fail — concrete fix: compare structurally (strip `Span` fields while walking `Program`/`Expr`/`Stmt`) instead of string-surgery on `format!("{:?}")`.
5. [MAJOR] tests/formatter_test.rs:971 — `edge_a_very_deeply_nested_program_is_handled_or_reported` uses depth 60, always below `MAX_NESTING_DEPTH`/`MAX_BLOCK_DEPTH` of 64 (src/parser.rs:243), so the `Err` branch is never taken — why it matters: the resource-limit error path is claimed covered but untested — concrete fix: add a depth-70+ case asserting a clean `Parser error`, keeping the depth-60 idempotence case.
REVIEW VERDICT: FINDINGS 5
